## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical concurrency control under heavy load, enforcing per-team ordering with a global bottleneck and deterministic degradation. It assesses backpressure signaling, dynamic policy design, and test plan creation for real-world streaming workloads.

## Key Concepts

- Bounded global queue with capacity enforcement
- Per-team FIFO buffers maintaining sequence order
- Backpressure signaling mechanism to upstream producers
- Deterministic drop policy by severity level
- Ordering guarantees under graceful degradation
- Comprehensive test strategy for correctness and resilience

## Data Structures

```javascript
// Core types
type LogLevel = 'INFO' | 'WARN' | 'ERROR';
type Log = { teamId: string; severity: LogLevel; timestamp: number; payload: any; seq: number };

// Per-team FIFO buffer with sequence tracking
class TeamBuffer {
  constructor(teamId, capacity) {
    this.teamId = teamId;
    this.buffer = [];  // Circular buffer or ring buffer
    this.seq = 0;       // Monotonic sequence number
    this.criticalSeq = 0;  // Highest preserved ERROR/WARN seq
  }

  push(log) {
    log.seq = this.seq++;
    this.buffer.push(log);
  }

  // Deterministic drop: remove oldest non-critical when over capacity
  prune(threshold) {
    // Keep all ERROR, keep most recent WARN, drop oldest INFO
  }
}

// Global bounded queue with backpressure signal
class LogIngestionPipeline {
  constructor(globalCapacity, backlogThreshold) {
    this.globalQueue = new Map();  // teamId -> TeamBuffer
    this.capacity = globalCapacity;
    this.backlogThreshold = backlogThreshold;
    this.currentBacklog = 0;
  }

  // Backpressure: signal when approaching threshold
  isBacklogged() {
    return this.currentBacklog >= this.backlogThreshold;
  }

  ingest(log) {
    if (!this.globalQueue.has(log.teamId)) {
      this.globalQueue.set(log.teamId, new TeamBuffer(log.teamId));
    }

    const buffer = this.globalQueue.get(log.teamId);

    // Always accept ERROR logs
    if (log.severity === 'ERROR') {
      buffer.push(log);
      this.currentBacklog++;
      return true;
    }

    // Under backlog: accept all
    if (!this.isBacklogged()) {
      buffer.push(log);
      this.currentBacklog++;
      return true;
    }

    // Over backlog: deterministic drop policy
    return buffer.tryAppendWithPruning(log, this.backlogThreshold / this.globalQueue.size);
  }
}
```

## Backpressure Signaling

- **Push-based**: Callback/EventEmitter to producers when backlog > 80% threshold
- **Pull-based**: Expose `canAccept()` or `backlogPercentage()` for producers to poll
- **HTTP headers**: X-RateLimit headers (Retry-After, X-Backlog-Level)
- **Circuit breaker**: Temporarily reject with 503 Service Unavailable

## Test Plan

### Unit Tests
1. **Ordering verification**: Confirm per-team logs maintain FIFO order under normal and degraded conditions
2. **Drop policy correctness**: Verify ERROR logs never dropped; INFO/WARN dropped deterministically when over threshold
3. **Backpressure triggers**: Validate signal fires at correct threshold
4. **Sequence integrity**: Ensure seq numbers preserved after pruning

### Integration Tests
1. **High throughput**: Simulate 10x normal load, verify graceful degradation
2. **Burst handling**: Rapid bursts per team, confirm fair buffer management
3. **Recovery**: Backlog clears, verify no log loss or corruption

### Chaos Tests
1. **Producer failure**: Stop producers mid-stream, verify pipeline stability
2. **Memory pressure**: Constrain heap, verify bounded behavior
3. **Ordering stress**: Random severity injection, validate final order
